-japans-tsunami-victims-opens-at-lithuanian-foreign-ministry:3249"}, {"title": "hideakis exhibition to commemorate japans tsunami victims:31020", "url": "https://www.urm.lt/en/news/928/hideakis-exhibition-to-commemorate-japans-tsunami-victims:31020"}, {"title": "hideakis exhibition to commemorate japans tsunami victims:31020", "url": "https://www.mfa.lt/en/news/928/hideakis-exhibition-to-commemorate-japans-tsunami-victims:31020"}, {"title": "hideakis exhibition to commemorate japans tsunami victims:3241", "url": "https://mission-vienna-io.mfa.lt/en/news/19/hideakis-exhibition-to-commemorate-japans-tsunami-victims:3241"}, {"title": "press y240727", "url": "https://www.artm.pref.hyogo.jp/news/press/pdf/press_y240727.pdf"}, {"title": "Posted:Mar 26, 2021", "url": "https://tokyoartbeat.com/en/articles/-/artists-and-the-disaster-imagining-in-the-10th-year"}, {"title": "masamitsuaraki.format.com", "url": "https://masamitsuaraki.format.com/12793046"}]}, "I didn't find a page that names the「いつかの、だれかに」展 directly, but one result looks closely related.\n\nA 2017 Kobe Shimbun feature describes 震災の研究グループ〔記憶・歴史・表現〕フォーラムのメンバー、蘇理剛志は十年前の地震で小学六年生の弟を亡くした. The brother's home in Higashinada-ku, Kobe was destroyed, and the 12-year-old died when falling roof parts and furniture struck him. The same article's photo caption refers to 1万1千字の言葉が亡くなった小学生の面影を伝える at CAP HOUSE in Chuo-ku, Kobe. That suggests a text-based installation about the boy, but the article doesn't use the exhibition title, so I can't confirm it's the same work.\n\nOther results were unrelated: a Hyogo Prefectural Museum of Art 2024–25 exhibition on the 30th anniversary of the Hanshin earthquake, and a 2011 sound installation by Masamitsu Araki about a blind Fukushima resident. To confirm the exhibition, search the title with「CAP HOUSE」or「蘇理剛志」."], "durationSeconds": 5.540921958, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01QidyvJVo3h2B7wEPbfz4Qe", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", 